ily%3D%22Arial%22%20font-size%3D%2214%22%20fill%3D%22%23334155%22%3E05-05%2015%3A30%20UTC%3C%2Ftext%3E%0A%20%20%3Ctext%20x%3D%221010%22%20y%3D%22333%22%20font-family%3D%22Arial%22%20font-size%3D%2214%22%20font-weight%3D%22700%22%20fill%3D%22%23fb923c%22%3E0.00%25%3C%2Ftext%3E%0A%20%20%3Ctext%20x%3D%221112%22%20y%3D%22333%22%20font-family%3D%22Arial%22%20font-size%3D%2214%22%20fill%3D%22%2394a3b8%22%3E0%3C%2Ftext%3E%0A%3C%2Fsvg%3E%0A" alt="Application Insights list view screenshot"></p>
<p>The list view shows the same chart data in rows.</p>
<p>Use list view when you need exact values.</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Column</th>
<th>Meaning</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody><tr>
<td>Time</td>
<td>Time bucket for that row.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Requests</td>
<td>Number of requests during that time.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Errors</td>
<td>Number of errors during that time.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>P95 latency</td>
<td>Slow response time during that time.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Error rate</td>
<td>Failure percentage during that time.</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>How to check errors from list view:</p>
<ol>
<li>Click the <strong>List</strong> icon on the chart.</li>
<li>Find the row where <strong>Errors</strong> is more than 0.</li>
<li>Note the <strong>Time</strong> value.</li>
<li>Check the <strong>Error rate</strong> for the same row.</li>
<li>Open <strong>Workflow Analysis</strong> and search for failed workflows around that time.</li>
</ol>
<h3>How To Read Charts</h3>
<p>All charts are read in the same basic way:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Chart Part</th>
<th>Meaning</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody><tr>
<td>X axis</td>
<td>Time. Read from left to right to see when something happened.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Y axis</td>
<td>The value being measured, such as requests, errors, latency, or error rate.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Line going up</td>
<td>The value increased at that time.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Line going down</td>
<td>The value decreased at that time.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Spike</td>
<td>A sudden increase. Spikes are usually the first place to check.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Chart button</td>
<td>Shows the graph view.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>List button</td>
<td>Shows the same data in table format. Use this when you want exact values.</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>To check errors from any chart:</p>
<ol>
<li>Find the time where the line spikes.</li>
<li>Hover on that point to see the time and value.</li>
<li>If the chart or list shows an <strong>Errors</strong> value, click that time row or point to open the error details.</li>
<li>If error details are not enough, open <strong>Workflow Analysis</strong> and check failed workflows around the same time.</li>
</ol>
