<p>The <strong>Requests</strong> chart shows how much traffic the app received.</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Axis</th>
<th>Meaning</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody><tr>
<td>X axis</td>
<td>Time.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Y axis</td>
<td>Number of requests.</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>How to check:</p>
<ol>
<li>Look for a sudden increase in requests.</li>
<li>Check whether errors also increased at the same time.</li>
<li>If requests are high but errors are low, the app is handling traffic normally.</li>
<li>If requests and errors both increase, open the <strong>Errors</strong> chart and check the same time.</li>
</ol>
