%23111827%22%2F%3E%0A%20%20%3Ctext%20x%3D%22624%22%20y%3D%22102%22%20font-family%3D%22Arial%2C%20sans-serif%22%20font-size%3D%2213%22%20fill%3D%22%23ffffff%22%3E12%3A45%3C%2Ftext%3E%0A%20%20%3Ctext%20x%3D%22624%22%20y%3D%22123%22%20font-family%3D%22Arial%2C%20sans-serif%22%20font-size%3D%2213%22%20fill%3D%22%23ffffff%22%3EP95%3A%201930%20ms%3C%2Ftext%3E%0A%20%20%3Ctext%20x%3D%2232%22%20y%3D%22400%22%20font-family%3D%22Arial%2C%20sans-serif%22%20font-size%3D%2213%22%20fill%3D%22%236b7280%22%3ETeal%20line%20%3D%20P95%20latency.%20Grey%20line%20%3D%20average%20latency.%3C%2Ftext%3E%0A%3C%2Fsvg%3E%0A" alt="P95 latency chart screenshot"></p>
<p>The <strong>P95 Latency</strong> chart shows slow response time for the slowest group of users.</p>
<p>P95 means 95% of requests were faster than this value, and 5% were slower.</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Axis</th>
<th>Meaning</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody><tr>
<td>X axis</td>
<td>Time.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Y axis</td>
<td>Response time in milliseconds.</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>How to check:</p>
<ol>
<li>Look for a latency spike.</li>
<li>Hover on the spike to see the time and latency value.</li>
<li>Check whether errors increased at the same time.</li>
<li>If latency is high but errors are low, users may see slowness but requests may still be completing.</li>
<li>If latency and errors both increase, investigate the app and failed workflows for that time.</li>
</ol>
