20fill%3D%22%23ffffff%22%3EError%20rate%3A%207.1%25%3C%2Ftext%3E%0A%20%20%3Ctext%20x%3D%22624%22%20y%3D%22148%22%20font-family%3D%22Arial%2C%20sans-serif%22%20font-size%3D%2213%22%20fill%3D%22%23ffffff%22%3EErrors%3A%2033%3C%2Ftext%3E%0A%20%20%3Ctext%20x%3D%2232%22%20y%3D%22400%22%20font-family%3D%22Arial%2C%20sans-serif%22%20font-size%3D%2213%22%20fill%3D%22%236b7280%22%3EOrange%20line%20%3D%20error%20percentage%20for%20each%20time%20bucket.%3C%2Ftext%3E%0A%3C%2Fsvg%3E%0A" alt="Error rate chart screenshot"></p>
<p>The <strong>Error Rate</strong> chart shows what percentage of requests failed.</p>
<p>This is often more useful than total errors because it compares errors with traffic.</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Axis</th>
<th>Meaning</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody><tr>
<td>X axis</td>
<td>Time.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Y axis</td>
<td>Error percentage.</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>How to check:</p>
<ol>
<li>Look for the highest percentage spike.</li>
<li>Hover on the spike to see the error rate.</li>
<li>Switch to <strong>List</strong> view if you need the exact percentage.</li>
<li>Check the <strong>Errors</strong> chart for the same time.</li>
<li>Open <strong>Workflow Analysis</strong> if the error rate spike matches workflow failures.</li>
</ol>
<h3>Simple Chart Example</h3>
<p>If the <strong>Errors</strong> chart spikes at 12:45:</p>
<ol>
<li>Check the <strong>Requests</strong> chart at 12:45.</li>
<li>If requests also spiked, the errors may be traffic-related.</li>
<li>Check the <strong>Error Rate</strong> chart at 12:45.</li>
<li>If error rate is also high, the app has a real failure issue.</li>
<li>Open <strong>Workflow Analysis</strong>, filter by <strong>Failed</strong>, and check workflows started around 12:45.</li>
</ol>
<h3>How to Check App Health</h3>
<ol>
<li>Open the app from Dashboard or Tenant And Apps.</li>
<li>Select the correct <strong>Environment</strong>.</li>
<li>Select the correct <strong>Date Range</strong>.</li>
<li>Check <strong>Health Score</strong>, <strong>Total Errors</strong>, and <strong>Error Rate</strong>.</li>
<li>Check <strong>P95 Latency</strong> if users reported slowness.</li>
<li>Open <strong>Workflow Analysis</strong> if workflow failures are shown.</li>
</ol>
<hr>
<h2>4. Workflow Analysis Page</h2>
<h3>What This Page Is</h3>
<p>The <strong>Workflow Analysis</strong> page shows workflow executions for the selected app.</p>
<p>Use this page when you want to find failed, running, or completed workflows.</p>
