e1%22%3Ez396791638954%3C%2Ftext%3E%0A%20%20%20%20%3Ctext%20x%3D%2286%22%20y%3D%22371%22%20font-size%3D%2215%22%20fill%3D%22%2393c5fd%22%3EStep%20failed%20to%20prepare%20POST%20request%20due%20to%20unresolved%20expression%20dependency%3C%2Ftext%3E%0A%20%20%20%20%3Ccircle%20cx%3D%2262%22%20cy%3D%22440%22%20r%3D%228%22%20fill%3D%22%23ef4444%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2259%22%20y%3D%22444%22%20font-size%3D%2210%22%20fill%3D%22%23fff%22%3E4%3C%2Ftext%3E%0A%20%20%20%20%3Ctext%20x%3D%2286%22%20y%3D%22442%22%20font-size%3D%2216%22%20font-weight%3D%22700%22%20fill%3D%22%23fff%22%3EWorkflow%20failure%3C%2Ftext%3E%0A%20%20%20%20%3Ctext%20x%3D%2286%22%20y%3D%22466%22%20font-size%3D%2215%22%20fill%3D%22%2393c5fd%22%3EWorkflow%20marked%20as%20FAILED%20with%20NonExistingLiteral%20error%20in%20post_documents%20step%3C%2Ftext%3E%0A%20%20%3C%2Fg%3E%0A%3C%2Fsvg%3E%0A" alt="Failure chain screenshot"></p>
<p>The <strong>Failure Chain</strong> explains the failure step by step.</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Part</th>
<th>Meaning</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody><tr>
<td>Step number</td>
<td>Order in which the failure happened.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Step name</td>
<td>Workflow step or action name.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Step ID</td>
<td>Internal workflow step ID.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Description</td>
<td>What happened in that step.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Temporal Event</td>
<td>Evidence from workflow event data.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Source panel</td>
<td>Shows where the evidence came from.</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>How to use the failure chain:</p>
<ol>
<li>Read from step 1 to the last step.</li>
<li>Find the first step where the real problem started.</li>
<li>Open the evidence panel if available.</li>
<li>Use the last step to confirm why the workflow was marked as failed.</li>
</ol>
<p>In the screenshot, the chain shows:</p>
<ol>
<li><code>post_documents</code> tried to run with <code>${loanNumber}</code>.</li>
<li>CEL expression evaluation could not find <code>${loanNumber}</code>.</li>
<li>API call preparation failed.</li>
<li>The workflow was marked as failed.</li>
</ol>
