3E%0A%20%20%20%20%3Ctext%20x%3D%2232%22%20y%3D%22181%22%20font-weight%3D%22700%22%20fill%3D%22%2392400e%22%3EAuthorization%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22150%22%20y%3D%22181%22%20font-family%3D%22Courier%20New%22%3EBearer%20%26lt%3Btoken%26gt%3B%3C%2Ftext%3E%0A%20%20%20%20%3Ctext%20x%3D%2232%22%20y%3D%22208%22%20font-weight%3D%22700%22%20fill%3D%22%2392400e%22%3EOrigin%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22150%22%20y%3D%22208%22%20font-family%3D%22Courier%20New%22%3Ehttps%3A%2F%2Fnewui-paidloan.alerusapps.live...%3C%2Ftext%3E%0A%20%20%20%20%3Ctext%20x%3D%2232%22%20y%3D%22235%22%20font-weight%3D%22700%22%20fill%3D%22%2392400e%22%3EUser-Agent%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22150%22%20y%3D%22235%22%20font-family%3D%22Courier%20New%22%3EMozilla%2F5.0%20Chrome%2F147.0.0.0%3C%2Ftext%3E%0A%20%20%20%20%3Ctext%20x%3D%2232%22%20y%3D%22262%22%20font-weight%3D%22700%22%20fill%3D%22%2392400e%22%3EAccept%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22150%22%20y%3D%22262%22%20font-family%3D%22Courier%20New%22%3Eapplication%2Fjson%2C%20text%2Fplain%2C%20*%2F*%3C%2Ftext%3E%0A%20%20%3C%2Fg%3E%0A%20%20%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%22316%22%20font-family%3D%22Arial%22%20font-size%3D%2211%22%20font-weight%3D%22700%22%20fill%3D%22%2392400e%22%3EBODY%20%2F%20PARAMS%3C%2Ftext%3E%0A%20%20%3Crect%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%22332%22%20width%3D%22390%22%20height%3D%22165%22%20rx%3D%226%22%20fill%3D%22%23fffbeb%22%20stroke%3D%22%23facc15%22%2F%3E%0A%20%20%3Cg%20font-family%3D%22Arial%22%20font-size%3D%2212%22%3E%0A%20%20%20%20%3Ctext%20x%3D%2232%22%20y%3D%22354%22%20font-weight%3D%22700%22%20fill%3D%22%23047857%22%3E_fields%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22150%22%20y%3D%22354%22%20font-family%3D%22Courier%20New%22%3Eid%3C%2Ftext%3E%0A%20%20%20%20%3Ctext%20x%3D%2232%22%20y%3D%22381%22%20font-weight%3D%22700%22%20fill%3D%22%23047857%22%3Esys.genAppHost%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22150%22%20y%3D%22381%22%20font-family%3D%22Courier%20New%22%3Ehttp%3A%2F%2Fapp-data-manager%3A8002%3C%2Ftext%3E%0A%20%20%20%20%3Ctext%20x%3D%2232%22%20y%3D%22408%22%20font-weight%3D%22700%22%20fill%3D%22%23047857%22%3Esys.platformUrl%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22150%22%20y%3D%22408%22%20font-family%3D%22Courier%20New%22%3Ehttps%3A%2F%2Flive.jiffy.ai%3C%2Ftext%3E%0A%20%20%20%20%3Ctext%20x%3D%2232%22%20y%3D%22435%22%20font-weight%3D%22700%22%20fill%3D%22%23047857%22%3Esys.workflowHash%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22150%22%20y%3D%22435%22%20font-family%3D%22Courier%20New%22%3E4208fde0703ae8e24a4a...%3C%2Ftext%3E%0A%20%20%20%20%3Ctext%20x%3D%2232%22%20y%3D%22462%22%20font-weight%3D%22700%22%20fill%3D%22%23047857%22%3Esys.workflowVersion%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22150%22%20y%3D%22462%22%20font-family%3D%22Courier%20New%22%3E1.0.0%3C%2Ftext%3E%0A%20%20%3C%2Fg%3E%0A%3C%2Fsvg%3E%0A" alt="Workflow request details screenshot"></p>
<p>The request details panel shows the HTTP request that triggered or supported the workflow step.</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Field</th>
<th>Meaning</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody><tr>
<td>Method</td>
<td>HTTP method, such as POST.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>URL</td>
<td>API endpoint called.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Copy cURL</td>
<td>Copies the request as a cURL command.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Headers</td>
<td>Request metadata, such as content type, origin, user agent, and authorization.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Body / Params</td>
<td>Input values sent with the request.</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>How to check request details:</p>
<ol>
<li>Confirm the <strong>Method</strong> and <strong>URL</strong>.</li>
<li>Check <strong>Body / Params</strong> for missing or wrong values.</li>
<li>Check <strong>Headers</strong> if the issue may be related to authorization, origin, or content type.</li>
<li>Use <strong>Copy cURL</strong> only when a developer needs to reproduce the request.</li>
</ol>
<h3>What You Can See</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Section</th>
<th>Meaning</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody><tr>
<td>Status</td>
<td>Shows whether the workflow failed, completed, or is running.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Workflow ID</td>
<td>Unique ID of the workflow.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Started At</td>
<td>Time the workflow started.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Process Name</td>
<td>Workflow process name.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Complete Error</td>
<td>Full error message and stack trace if available.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Root Cause Analysis</td>
<td>Simple explanation of why the workflow failed.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Suggested Fix</td>
<td>Recommended steps to fix the issue.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Failure Chain</td>
<td>Step-by-step path that led to the failure.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Evidence Logs</td>
<td>Logs related to the failed workflow.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Previously Applied Fixes</td>
<td>Past fixes for similar errors, if available.</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
<h3>How to Use Investigation Details</h3>
<ol>
<li>Read the <strong>Complete Error</strong> first.</li>
<li>Read the <strong>Root Cause Analysis</strong>.</li>
<li>Check the <strong>Failure Chain</strong> to understand where it failed.</li>
<li>Open evidence logs if you need proof from logs.</li>
<li>Follow the <strong>Suggested Fix</strong>.</li>
<li>If you fixed the issue, submit the fix so others can reuse it later.</li>
</ol>
<hr>
<h2>6. Quick Checks</h2>
<h3>If A Tenant Looks Critical</h3>
<ol>
<li>Open <strong>Dashboard</strong>.</li>
<li>Select the correct date range and environment.</li>
<li>Click the tenant.</li>
<li>Check which app has high errors.</li>
<li>Open that app&#39;s <strong>Application Insights</strong>.</li>
</ol>
<h3>If An App Has Errors</h3>
<ol>
<li>Open <strong>Application Insights</strong>.</li>
<li>Check <strong>Total Errors</strong> and <strong>Error Rate</strong>.</li>
<li>Check the error chart to see when errors started.</li>
<li>Open <strong>Workflow Analysis</strong> if workflow failures exist.</li>
</ol>
<h3>If Users Report Slowness</h3>
<ol>
<li>Open the app in <strong>Application Insights</strong>.</li>
<li>Check <strong>Average Latency</strong> and <strong>P95 Latency</strong>.</li>
<li>Check the latency chart.</li>
<li>Change the date range to find when slowness started.</li>
</ol>
<h3>If A Workflow Failed</h3>
<ol>
<li>Open <strong>Workflow Analysis</strong>.</li>
<li>Filter by <strong>Failed</strong>.</li>
<li>Search by workflow ID or process name.</li>
<li>Click <strong>Investigate</strong>.</li>
<li>Read root cause, logs, and suggested fix.</li>
</ol>
<hr>
<h2>7. Simple Status Meaning</h2>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Status / Color</th>
<th>Meaning</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody><tr>
<td>Green / Healthy</td>
<td>Working normally.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Yellow / Warning</td>
<td>Some issues are present. Check errors and latency.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Red / Critical</td>
<td>Many failures or poor health. Investigate quickly.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Failed</td>
<td>Workflow did not complete successfully.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Running</td>
<td>Workflow is still in progress.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Completed</td>
<td>Workflow finished successfully.</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
<hr>
<h2>8. Basic Troubleshooting</h2>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Problem</th>
<th>What To Do</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody><tr>
<td>Dashboard data looks old</td>
<td>Check <strong>Last Updated</strong> and refresh the page.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Error rate is high</td>
<td>Open the app and check Application Insights.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Workflow failures are high</td>
<td>Open Workflow Analysis and filter by Failed.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>App looks slow</td>
<td>Check Average Latency and P95 Latency.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Cannot find a workflow</td>
<td>Increase the date range or search by Workflow ID.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Investigation has no result</td>
<td>The workflow details may not be available anymore. Use error message and logs if shown.</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
<hr>
<h2>9. Best Way To Use The App</h2>
<p>For most checks, follow this order:</p>
<ol>
<li>Start from <strong>Dashboard</strong>.</li>
<li>Find the tenant or app with high errors.</li>
<li>Open <strong>Application Insights</strong>.</li>
<li>Check errors, error rate, health, and latency.</li>
<li>Open <strong>Workflow Analysis</strong> for failed workflows.</li>
<li>Click <strong>Investigate</strong> to understand the failure.</li>
</ol>

</body>
</html>
